{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-122937" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following are partitions of the real interval $[-3,7]?$\n\n- ${-3,-5,1,2,6}$\n- ${-3,0,3,7,8}$\n- ${-3,-2,1,3,4,7}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122937" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A partition $P$ of a closed interval $[a,b]$ is a finite sequence of real numbers taken from $[a,b]$ such that\n\n$$\na={x}_{0}<{x}_{1}<{x}_{2}<…<{x}_{n}=b\\,.\n$$\n\nWe can express $P$ using set notation as\n\n$$\nP={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{n}}.\n$$\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement:\n\n- Statement I is not a partition of $[-3,7]$ since it does not include the right endpoint $b=7.$\n\n- Statement II is not a partition of $[-3,7]$ since $8$ does not belong to $[-3,7].$\n\n- Statement III is a partition of $[-3,7].$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122937" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0d6c3233ed270376fb0b9c4f059a52329d883f23538b5b1303390ad81f555b7a"} {"question" "q-122937" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0