int $b=6.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements give a partition of  $[-4,6].$\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122932" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0d6c3233ed270376fb0b9c4f059a52329d883f23538b5b1303390ad81f555b7a"} {"question" "q-122932" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122932" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "None of the statements give a partition of  $[-4,6]$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122932" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "None of the statements give a partition of  $[-4,6]$"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122954" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following are partitions of the real interval $[-1,1]?$\n\n- $-1<0<\\frac{1}{2}<1$\n- ${-2,-1,0,1}$\n- ${-1,0,2}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122954" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A partition $P$ of a closed interval $[a,b]$ is a finite sequence of real numbers taken from $[a,b]$ such that\n\n$$\na={x}_{0}<{x}_{1}<{x}_{2}<…<{x}_{n}=b\\,.\n$$\n\nWe can express $P$ using set notation as\n\n$$\nP={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{n}}.\n$$\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement:\n\n- Statement I is a partition of $[-1,1].$\n\n- Statement II is not a partition of $[-1,1]$ since $-2$ does not belong to $[-1,1].$\n\n- Statement III is not a partition of  $[-1,1]$ since $2$ does not belong to $[-1,1].$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122954" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0d6c3233ed270376fb0b9c4f059a52329d883f23538b5b1303390ad81f555b7a"} {"question" "q-122954" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122954" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"] ["text" "None of the statements give a partition of $[-1,1]$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122954" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122935" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following are partitions of the real interval $[-10,-2]?$\n\n- ${-10,-9,-8,-4,-2}$\n- ${-9,-5,-4,-2}$\n- $-10<-6<-4<-3$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122935" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A partition $P$ of a closed interval $[a,b]$ is a finite sequence of real numbers taken from $[a,b]$ such that\n\n$$\na={x}_{0}<{x}_{1}<{x}_{2}<…<{x}_{n}=b\\,.\n$$\n\nWe can express $P$ using set notation as\n\n$$\nP={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{n}}.\n$$\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement:\n\n- Statement I is a partition of $[-10,-2].$\n\n- Statement II is not a partition of $[-10,-2]$  since it does not include the left endpoint $a=-10.$\n\n- Statement III is not a partition of $[-10,-2]$ since it does not include the right endpoint $b=-2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122935" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0d6c3233ed270376fb0b9c4f059a52329d883f23538b5b1303390ad81f555b7a"} {"question" "q-122935" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122935" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"] ["text" "None of the statements give a partition of $[-10,-2]$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122935" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122938" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following are partitions of the real interval $[0,4]?$\n\n- $0<0.5<1.5<2.5<4<4.5$\n- ${0,1,2,3.9}$\n- $0<0.1<1.5<2.5<4$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122938" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A partition $P$ of a closed interval $[a,b]$ is a finite sequence of real numbers taken from $[a,b]$ such that\n\n$$\na={x}_{0}<{x}_{1}<{x}_{2}<…<{x}_{n}=b\\,.\n$$\n\nWe can express $P$ using set notation as\n\n$$\nP={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{n}}.\n$$\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement:\n\n- Statement I is not a partition of $[0,4]$  since $4.5$ does not belong to $[0,4].$\n\n- Statement II is not a partition of $[0,4]$  since it does not include the left endpoint $a=4.$\n\n- Statement III is  a partition of  $[0,4].$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122938" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0d6c3233ed270376fb0b9c4f059a52329d883f23538b5b1303390ad81f555b7a"} {"question" "q-122938" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122938" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"] ["text" "None of the statements give a partition of $[0,4]$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122938" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122979" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $P={{z}_{0},{z}_{1},…,{z}_{q}}$ be a partition of the interval $[4,9].$ If $Δ{z}_{k}={z}_{k}-{z}_{k-1},$ calculate ${\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}7Δ{z}_{k}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122979" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we take the factor $7$ outside the summation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}7Δ{z}_{k}=7{\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}Δ{z}_{k}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that ${\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}Δ{z}_{k}$ is just the length of the interval $[4,9],$ because\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}Δ{z}_{k} & =({z}_{1}-{z}_{0})+({z}_{2}-{z}_{1})+({z}_{3}-{z}_{2})+⋯+({z}_{q}-{z}_{q-1}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{z}_{1}}-{z}_{0})+(\\cancel{{z}_{2}}-\\cancel{{z}_{1}})+(\\cancel{{z}_{3}}-\\cancel{{z}_{2}})+⋯+({z}_{q}-\\cancel{{z}_{q-1}}) \\\\  & =-{z}_{0}+{z}_{q} \\\\  & ={z}_{q}-{z}_{0} \\\\  & =9-4 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n7{\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}Δ{z}_{k}=7\\cdot 5=35.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122979" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0d6c3233ed270376fb0b9c4f059a52329d883f23538b5b1303390ad81f555b7a"} {"question" "q-122979" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122979" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "14"] ["math" "21"] ["math" "28"] ["math" "35"] ["math" "42"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122979" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "35"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122977" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $P={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}}$ be a partition of the interval $[2,10].$ If $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1},$ calculate ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}-4Δ{x}_{i}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122977" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we take the factor $(-4)$ outside the summation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}-4Δ{x}_{i}=-4{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}$ is just the length of the interval $[2,10],$ because\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i} & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{0})+({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})+({x}_{3}-{x}_{2})+⋯+({x}_{m}-{x}_{m-1}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{x}_{1}}-{x}_{0})+(\\cancel{{x}_{2}}-\\cancel{{x}_{1}})+(\\cancel{{x}_{3}}-\\cancel{{x}_{2}})+⋯+({x}_{m}-\\cancel{{x}_{m-1}}) \\\\  & =-{x}_{0}+{x}_{m} \\\\  & ={x}_{m}-{x}_{0} \\\\  & =10-2 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n-4{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}=(-4)\\cdot 8=-32.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122977" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0d6c3233ed270376fb0b9c4f059a52329d883f23538b5b1303390ad81f555b7a"} {"question" "q-122977" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122977" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-20"] ["math" "-24"] ["math" "-32"] ["math" "28"] ["math" "36"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122977" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-32"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122848" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $P={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}}$ be a partition of the interval $[0,3].$ If $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1},$ calculate ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}5Δ{x}_{i}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122848" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the constant multiple rule, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}5Δ{x}_{i}=5{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}$ is just the length of the interval $[0,3],$ because\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i} & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{0})+({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})+({x}_{3}-{x}_{2})+⋯+({x}_{m}-{x}_{m-1}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{x}_{1}}-{x}_{0})+(\\cancel{{x}_{2}}-\\cancel{{x}_{1}})+(\\cancel{{x}_{3}}-\\cancel{{x}_{2}})+⋯+({x}_{m}-\\cancel{{x}_{m-1}}) \\\\  & =-{x}_{0}+{x}_{m} \\\\  & ={x}_{m}-{x}_{0} \\\\  & =3-0 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n5{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}=5\\cdot 3=15.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122848" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0d6c3233ed270376fb0b9c4f059a52329d883f23538b5b1303390ad81f555b7a"} {"question" "q-122848" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122848" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10"] ["math" "15"] ["math" "20"] ["math" "25"] ["math" "5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122848" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "15"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122976" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $P={{z}_{0},{z}_{1},…,{z}_{q}}$ be a partition of the interval $[-7,-1].$ If $Δ{z}_{k}={z}_{k}-{z}_{k-1},$ calculate ${\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}Δ{z}_{k}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122976" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that ${\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}Δ{z}_{k}$ is just the length of the interval $[-7,-1],$ because\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}Δ{z}_{k} & =({z}_{1}-{z}_{0})+({z}_{2}-{z}_{1})+({z}_{3}-{z}_{2})+⋯+({z}_{q}-{z}_{q-1}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{z}_{1}}-{z}_{0})+(\\cancel{{z}_{2}}-\\cancel{{z}_{1}})+(\\cancel{{z}_{3}}-\\cancel{{z}_{2}})+⋯+({z}_{q}-\\cancel{{z}_{q-1}}) \\\\  & =-{z}_{0}+{z}_{q} \\\\  & ={z}_{q}-{z}_{0} \\\\  & =(-1)-(-7) \\\\  & =7-1 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122976" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0d6c3233ed270376fb0b9c4f059a52329d883f23538b5b1303390ad81f555b7a"} {"question" "q-122976" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122976" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-5"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "7"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122976" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122973" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $P={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}}$ be a partition of the interval $[4,11].$ If $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1},$ calculate ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122973" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}$ is just the length of the interval $[4,11],$ because\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i} & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{0})+({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})+({x}_{3}-{x}_{2})+⋯+({x}_{m}-{x}_{m-1}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{x}_{1}}-{x}_{0})+(\\cancel{{x}_{2}}-\\cancel{{x}_{1}})+(\\cancel{{x}_{3}}-\\cancel{{x}_{2}})+⋯+({x}_{m}-\\cancel{{x}_{m-1}}) \\\\  & =-{x}_{0}+{x}_{m} \\\\  & ={x}_{m}-{x}_{0} \\\\  & =11-4 \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122973" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0d6c3233ed270376fb0b9c4f059a52329d883f23538b5b1303390ad81f555b7a"} {"question" "q-122973" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122973" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "15"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "7"] ["math" "9"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122973" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "7"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122984" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $P={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}}$ be a partition of the interval $[1,5].$ If $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ calculate ${\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{y}_{j}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122984" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can simplify the given summation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{y}_{j} & =({y}_{1}+{y}_{0})Δ{y}_{1}+({y}_{2}+{y}_{1})Δ{y}_{2}+⋯+({y}_{n}+{y}_{n-1})Δ{y}_{n} \\\\  & =({y}_{1}+{y}_{0})({y}_{1}-{y}_{0})+({y}_{2}+{y}_{1})({y}_{2}-{y}_{1})+⋯+({y}_{n}+{y}_{n-1})({y}_{n}-{y}_{n-1}) \\\\  & =({y}_{1}^{2}-{y}_{0}^{2})+({y}_{2}^{2}-{y}_{1}^{2})+⋯+({y}_{n}^{2}-{y}_{n-1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{y}_{1}^{2}}-{y}_{0}^{2})+(\\cancel{{y}_{2}^{2}}-\\cancel{{y}_{1}^{2}})+⋯+({y}_{n}^{2}-\\cancel{{y}_{n-1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-{y}_{0}^{2}+{y}_{n}^{2} \\\\  & ={y}_{n}^{2}-{y}_{0}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since ${y}_{0}=1$ and ${y}_{n}=5$ are the endpoints of our partition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{y}_{i} & ={y}_{n}^{2}-{y}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & ={5}^{2}-{1}^{2} \\\\  & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122984" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0d6c3233ed270376fb0b9c4f059a52329d883f23538b5b1303390ad81f555b7a"} {"question" "q-122984" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122984" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "16"] ["math" "18"] ["math" "21"] ["math" "24"] ["math" "28"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122984" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "24"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122986" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $P={{z}_{0},{z}_{1},…,{z}_{q}}$ be a partition of the interval $[-2,2].$ If $Δ{z}_{k}={z}_{k}-{z}_{k-1},$ calculate ${\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}({z}_{k}+{z}_{k-1})Δ{z}_{k}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122986" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can simplify the given summation as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}({z}_{k}+{z}_{k-1})Δ{z}_{k} & =({z}_{1}+{z}_{0})Δ{z}_{1}+({z}_{2}+{z}_{1})Δ{z}_{2}+⋯+({z}_{q}+{z}_{q-1})Δ{z}_{n} \\\\  & =({z}_{1}+{z}_{0})({z}_{1}-{z}_{0})+({z}_{2}+{z}_{1})({z}_{2}-{z}_{1})+⋯+({z}_{q}+{z}_{q-1})({z}_{q}-{z}_{q-1}) \\\\  & =({z}_{1}^{2}-{z}_{0}^{2})+({z}_{2}^{2}-{z}_{1}^{2})+⋯+({z}_{q}^{2}-{z}_{q-1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{z}_{1}^{2}}-{z}_{0}^{2})+(\\cancel{{z}_{2}^{2}}-\\cancel{{z}_{1}^{2}})+⋯+({z}_{q}^{2}-\\cancel{{z}_{q-1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-{z}_{0}^{2}+{z}_{q}^{2} \\\\  & ={z}_{q}^{2}-{z}_{0}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since ${z}_{0}=-2$ and ${z}_{q}=2$ are the endpoints of our partition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}({z}_{k}+{z}_{k-1})Δ{z}_{k} & ={z}_{q}^{2}-{z}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & ={2}^{2}-(-2)^{2} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122986" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0d6c3233ed270376fb0b9c4f059a52329d883f23538b5b1303390ad81f555b7a"} {"question" "q-122986" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122986" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122986" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122849" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $P={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}}$ be a partition of the interval $[0,2].$ If $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1},$ calculate ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122849" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can simplify the given summation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i} & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{0})Δ{x}_{1}+({x}_{2}+{x}_{1})Δ{x}_{2}+⋯+({x}_{m}+{x}_{m-1})Δ{x}_{n} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{0})({x}_{1}-{x}_{0})+({x}_{2}+{x}_{1})({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})+⋯+({x}_{m}+{x}_{m-1})({x}_{m}-{x}_{m-1}) \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2})+({x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{1}^{2})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{m-1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}}-{x}_{0}^{2})+(\\cancel{{x}_{2}^{2}}-\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-\\cancel{{x}_{m-1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-{x}_{0}^{2}+{x}_{m}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since ${x}_{0}=0$ and ${x}_{m}=2$ are the endpoints of our partition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i} & ={x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & ={2}^{2}-{0}^{2} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122849" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0d6c3233ed270376fb0b9c4f059a52329d883f23538b5b1303390ad81f555b7a"} {"question" "q-122849" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122849" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122849" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122992" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $P={{z}_{0},{z}_{1},…,{z}_{q}}$ be a partition of the interval $[-2,4].$ If $Δ{z}_{k}={z}_{k}-{z}_{k-1},$ calculate ${\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}-2({z}_{k}+{z}_{k-1})Δ{z}_{k}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122992" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the constant multiple rule, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}-2({z}_{k}+{z}_{k-1})Δ{z}_{k}=-2{\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}({z}_{k}+{z}_{k-1})Δ{z}_{k}.\n$$\n\nWe can simplify the summation as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}({z}_{k}+{z}_{k-1})Δ{z}_{k} & =({z}_{1}+{z}_{0})Δ{z}_{1}+({z}_{2}+{z}_{1})Δ{z}_{2}+⋯+({z}_{q}+{z}_{q-1})Δ{z}_{n} \\\\  & =({z}_{1}+{z}_{0})({z}_{1}-{z}_{0})+({z}_{2}+{z}_{1})({z}_{2}-{z}_{1})+⋯+({z}_{q}+{z}_{q-1})({z}_{q}-{z}_{q-1}) \\\\  & =({z}_{1}^{2}-{z}_{0}^{2})+({z}_{2}^{2}-{z}_{1}^{2})+⋯+({z}_{q}^{2}-{z}_{q-1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{z}_{1}^{2}}-{z}_{0}^{2})+(\\cancel{{z}_{2}^{2}}-\\cancel{{z}_{1}^{2}})+⋯+({z}_{q}^{2}-\\cancel{{z}_{q-1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-{z}_{0}^{2}+{z}_{q}^{2} \\\\  & ={z}_{q}^{2}-{z}_{0}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since ${z}_{0}=-2$ and ${z}_{q}=4$ are the endpoints of our partition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}({z}_{k}+{z}_{k-1})Δ{z}_{k} & ={z}_{q}^{2}-{z}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & ={4}^{2}-(-2)^{2} \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n-2{\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}({z}_{k}+{z}_{k-1})Δ{z}_{k}=(-2)\\cdot 12=-24.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122992" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0d6c3233ed270376fb0b9c4f059a52329d883f23538b5b1303390ad81f555b7a"} {"question" "q-122992" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122992" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-12"] ["math" "-16"] ["math" "-20"] ["math" "-24"] ["math" "-28"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122992" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-24"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122988" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $P={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}}$ be a partition of the interval $[5,10].$ If $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ calculate ${\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{y}_{j}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122988" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can simplify the given summation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{y}_{j} & =({y}_{1}+{y}_{0})Δ{y}_{1}+({y}_{2}+{y}_{1})Δ{y}_{2}+⋯+({y}_{n}+{y}_{n-1})Δ{y}_{n} \\\\  & =({y}_{1}+{y}_{0})({y}_{1}-{y}_{0})+({y}_{2}+{y}_{1})({y}_{2}-{y}_{1})+⋯+({y}_{n}+{y}_{n-1})({y}_{n}-{y}_{n-1}) \\\\  & =({y}_{1}^{2}-{y}_{0}^{2})+({y}_{2}^{2}-{y}_{1}^{2})+⋯+({y}_{n}^{2}-{y}_{n-1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{y}_{1}^{2}}-{y}_{0}^{2})+(\\cancel{{y}_{2}^{2}}-\\cancel{{y}_{1}^{2}})+⋯+({y}_{n}^{2}-\\cancel{{y}_{n-1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-{y}_{0}^{2}+{y}_{n}^{2} \\\\  & ={y}_{n}^{2}-{y}_{0}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since ${y}_{0}=5$ and ${y}_{n}=10$ are the endpoints of our partition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{y}_{i} & ={y}_{n}^{2}-{y}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & ={10}^{2}-{5}^{2} \\\\  & =75.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122988" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0d6c3233ed270376fb0b9c4f059a52329d883f23538b5b1303390ad81f555b7a"} {"question" "q-122988" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122988" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "70"] ["math" "72"] ["math" "74"] ["math" "75"] ["math" "78"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "q-122988" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "75"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/state.json" "file_sha256" "1893983f0b2355685c043734bc9e65dd3fa0a1c13fa85edf0d9472bda2015eb8"} {"question" "e-9484" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following are partitions of the real interval $[1,9]?$\n\n- $\\{1, 4, 5, 8\\}$\n\n- $\\{1, 3, 4, 9\\}$\n\n- $1 <     2  <    9$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/example-9484.json" "file_sha256" "844140deb6fbefaece4c077b6b46d79719357e26fee34632bad0d0bf9030d7d8"} {"question" "e-9484" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A partition $P$ of a closed interval $[a,b]$ is a finite sequence of real numbers taken from $[a,b]$ such that\n\n$$\na = x_0 <      x_1<      x_2 <      \\ldots <      x_n = b\\,.\n$$\n\nWe can express $P$ using set notation as\n\n$$\nP=\\{x_0,x_1,\\ldots,x_n\\}.\n$$\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement:\n\n- Statement I is not a partition of $[1,9]$ since it does not include the right endpoint $b=9.$\n\n- Statement II is a partition of $[1,9].$\n\n- Statement III is a partition of $[1,9].$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/example-9484.json" "file_sha256" "844140deb6fbefaece4c077b6b46d79719357e26fee34632bad0d0bf9030d7d8"} {"question" "e-9480" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $P= \\left\\{y_0, y_1, \\ldots, y_n\\right\\}$ be a partition of the interval $[-3, 5].$ If $\\Delta y_j = y_j - y_{j-1},$ calculate $\\displaystyle \\sum_{j=1}^n {3}\\Delta y_j.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/example-9480.json" "file_sha256" "efe8a2abc6124505988cccaf6f3b434a86ae467fa061326175697412446e8653"} {"question" "e-9480" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we take the factor $3$ outside the summation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}3Δ{y}_{j}=3{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $\\displaystyle \\sum_{j=1}^n \\Delta y_j$ is just the length of the interval $[-3, 5],$ because\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j} & =Δ{y}_{1}+Δ{y}_{2}+Δ{y}_{3}+⋯+Δ{y}_{n} \\\\  & =({y}_{1}-{y}_{0})+({y}_{2}-{y}_{1})+({y}_{3}-{y}_{2})+⋯+({y}_{n}-{y}_{n-1}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{y}_{1}}-{y}_{0})+(\\cancel{{y}_{2}}-\\cancel{{y}_{1}})+(\\cancel{{y}_{3}}-\\cancel{{y}_{2}})+⋯+({y}_{n}-\\cancel{{y}_{n-1}}) \\\\  & =-{y}_{0}+{y}_{n} \\\\  & ={y}_{n}-{y}_{0} \\\\  & =5-(-3) \\\\  & =5+3 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{3}\\sum_{j=1}^n \\Delta y_j = 3 \\cdot 8 = 24.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/example-9480.json" "file_sha256" "efe8a2abc6124505988cccaf6f3b434a86ae467fa061326175697412446e8653"} {"question" "e-9481" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $P = \\left\\{x_0, x_1, \\ldots, x_m\\right\\}$ be a partition of the interval $[-3, 4].$ If $\\Delta x_i = x_i - x_{i-1},$ calculate $\\displaystyle\\sum_{i=1}^m (x_i + x_{i-1})\\Delta x_i .$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/example-9481.json" "file_sha256" "826c7a2f280007e137c79a964bd707ed2e9a5566e9f26dc59c89e662c596bd21"} {"question" "e-9481" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can simplify the given summation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i} & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{0})Δ{x}_{1}+({x}_{2}+{x}_{1})Δ{x}_{2}+⋯+({x}_{m}+{x}_{m-1})Δ{x}_{m} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{0})({x}_{1}-{x}_{0})+({x}_{2}+{x}_{1})({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})+⋯+({x}_{m}+{x}_{m-1})({x}_{m}-{x}_{m-1}) \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2})+({x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{1}^{2})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{m-1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}}-{x}_{0}^{2})+(\\cancel{{x}_{2}^{2}}-\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-\\cancel{{x}_{m-1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-{x}_{0}^{2}+{x}_{m}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $x_0 = -3$ and $x_m = 4$ are the endpoints of our partition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i} & ={x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & ={4}^{2}-(-3)^{2} \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072101/example-9481.json" "file_sha256" "826c7a2f280007e137c79a964bd707ed2e9a5566e9f26dc59c89e662c596bd21"}] "usage" {"e-9481" [] "e-9480" [] "e-9484" [] "q-122849" [] "q-122848" []} "basis" 2607 "retractions" [[17592186179905 :question/problem "Let $P = {x_{0}, x_{1}, …, x_{m}}$ be a partition of the interval $[0, 3]$. If $Δx_{i} = x_{i} - x_{i - 1}$, calculate $∑_(i = 1)^(m)5Δx_{i}$."] [17592186179906 :question/problem "Let $P = {x_{0}, x_{1}, …, x_{m}}$ be a partition of the interval $[0, 2]$. If $Δx_{i} = x_{i} - x_{i - 1}$, calculate $∑_(i = 1)^(m)(x_{i} + x_{i - 1})Δx_{i}$."] [17592186179515 :question/problem "Which of the following are partitions of the real interval $[1,9]$?\n\n1. $\\{1, 4, 5, 8\\}$\n2. $\\{1, 3, 4, 9\\}$\n3. $1 < 2 < 9$"] [17592186179515 :question/worked-solution "A partition $P$ of a closed interval $[a,b]$ is a finite sequence of real numbers taken from $[a,b]$ such that\n\n$$\na = x_0 < x_1< x_2 < \\ldots < x_n = b\\,\n$$\n\nWe can express $P$ using set notation as\n\n$$\nP=\\{x_0,x_1,\\ldots,x_n\\}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement:\n\n- Statement I is not a partition of $[1,9]$ since it does not include the right endpoint $b=9$.\n- Statement II is a partition of $[1,9]$.\n- Statement III is a partition of $[1,9]$.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""] [17592186179512 :question/problem "Let $P= \\left\\{y_0, y_1, \\ldots, y_n\\right\\}$ be a partition of the interval $[-3, 5]$. If $\\Delta y_j = y_j - y_{j-1}$, calculate $\\displaystyle \\sum_{j=1}^n {3}\\Delta y_j$."] [17592186179512 :question/worked-solution "First, we take the factor $3$ outside the summation:\n\n$$\n∑_(j = 1)^(n)3Δy_{j} = 3∑_(j = 1)^(n)Δy_{j}\n$$\n\nNote that\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\sum_{j=1}^n \\Delta y_j\n$$\n\nis just the length of the interval $[-3, 5]$, because\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∑_(j = 1)^(n)Δy_{j} &= Δy_{1} + Δy_{2} + Δy_{3} + ⋯ + Δy_{n} \\\\\n&= (y_{1} - y_{0}) + (y_{2} - y_{1}) + (y_{3} - y_{2}) + ⋯ + (y_{n} - y_{n - 1}) \\\\\n&= (y_{1} - y_{0}) + (y_{2} - y_{1}) + (y_{3} - y_{2}) + ⋯ + (y_{n} - y_{n - 1}) \\\\\n&=-y_{0} + y_{n} \\\\\n&= y_{n} - y_{0} \\\\\n&= 5 - (-3) \\\\\n&= 5 + 3 \\\\\n&= 8\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{3}\\sum_{j=1}^n \\Delta y_j = 3 \\cdot 8 = 24\n$$"] [17592186179513 :question/problem "Let $P = \\left\\{x_0, x_1, \\ldots, x_m\\right\\}$ be a partition of the interval $[-3, 4]$. If $\\Delta x_i = x_i - x_{i-1}$, calculate $\\displaystyle\\sum_{i=1}^m (x_i + x_{i-1})\\Delta x_i$."] [17592186179513 :question/worked-solution "We can simplify the given summation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∑_(i = 1)^(m)(x_{i} + x_{i - 1})Δx_{i} &= (x_{1} + x_{0})Δx_{1} + (x_{2} + x_{1})Δx_{2} + ⋯ + (x_{m} + x_{m - 1})Δx_{m} \\\\\n&= (x_{1} + x_{0})(x_{1} - x_{0}) + (x_{2} + x_{1})(x_{2} - x_{1}) + ⋯ + (x_{m} + x_{m - 1})(x_{m} - x_{m - 1}) \\\\\n&= (x_{1}^{2} - x_{0}^{2}) + (x_{2}^{2} - x_{1}^{2}) + ⋯ + (x_{m}^{2} - x_{m - 1}^{2}) \\\\\n&= (x_{1}^{2} - x_{0}^{2}) + (x_{2}^{2} - x_{1}^{2}) + ⋯ + (x_{m}^{2} - x_{m - 1}^{2}) \\\\\n&=-x_{0}^{2} + x_{m}^{2} \\\\\n&= x_{m}^{2} - x_{0}^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $x_0 = -3$ and $x_m = 4$ are the endpoints of our partition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∑_(i = 1)^(m)(x_{i} + x_{i - 1})Δx_{i} &= x_{m}^{2} - x_{0}^{2} \\\\\n&= 4^{2} - (-3)^{2} \\\\\n&= 7\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186177431 17592186177432 17592186177433 17592186177434 17592186177435 17592186177437 17592186177438 17592186177439 17592186177440 17592186177441] "immutable_fields" [[17592186177430 :answer-field/correct] [17592186177430 :answer-field/id] [17592186177430 :answer-field/key] [17592186177430 :answer-field/type] [17592186177436 :answer-field/correct] [17592186177436 :answer-field/id] [17592186177436 :answer-field/key] [17592186177436 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
